# Pokémon Shiny Hunt Randomizer

A simple browser-based randomizer for choosing Pokémon to shiny hunt across a collection of Pokémon games.

The project is designed to avoid duplicate species and only include Pokémon that can actually be shiny hunted in at least one supported game.

## Supported Games

- Pokémon Sword & Shield + DLC
- Pokémon Legends: Arceus
- Pokémon Scarlet & Violet + DLC
- Pokémon Legends: Z-A + Mega Dimension
- Pokémon FireRed — Nintendo Switch version

## Features

- Randomly selects a shiny-hunt target
- Uses one duplicate-free master list of Pokémon species
- Lets you enable or disable individual games
- Avoids rerolling the same Pokémon until the roll history is reset
- Displays the Pokémon's:
  - Hunt number
  - Name
  - National Pokédex number
  - Games in which it can be shiny hunted
  - General hunting method
- Displays:
  - Animated normal sprites from Pokémon Showdown
  - Shiny comparison sprites from Pokémon Database
- Remembers downloaded Pokédex data locally in the browser

## How the List Works

Pokémon are added to the master list in this order:

1. Sword & Shield
2. Legends: Arceus
3. Scarlet & Violet
4. Legends: Z-A
5. FireRed

If a Pokémon already exists in the list, it is not added again.

For example, if Pikachu is available in several supported games, Pikachu still receives only one hunt number.

The program also attempts to account for shiny-locked Pokémon and unusual hunt methods such as:

- Dynamax Adventures
- Mass Outbreaks
- Space-Time Distortions
- Legends: Z-A Special Scans
- Static legendary encounters
- FireRed Navel Rock and Birth Island encounters

## Using the Randomizer

Open the hosted webpage and select the games you want included.

Press **Randomize!** to choose a Pokémon.

The result will show which selected games can be used to hunt that Pokémon and a general description of how it can be obtained.

You can disable:

> Do not roll the same Pokémon twice until reset

if you want completely unrestricted random rolls.

## Data Sources

This project uses data and images from several external Pokémon resources:

- [PokéAPI](https://pokeapi.co/) — Pokédex and species data
- [Pokémon Showdown](https://pokemonshowdown.com/) — animated Pokémon sprites
- [Pokémon Database](https://pokemondb.net/) — shiny comparison sprites

Pokémon and all related names, characters, and imagery are trademarks of Nintendo, Game Freak, Creatures Inc., and The Pokémon Company.

This is an unofficial fan-made tool and is not affiliated with or endorsed by those companies.

## Project Status

This project is currently a small personal utility and is still being refined.

Planned or possible improvements include:

- Tracking completed shiny hunts
- Permanently excluding already-owned shinies
- More detailed hunting locations and methods
- Type information
- Better handling of alternate forms
- Additional games

## Hosting

The project is built entirely with HTML, CSS, and JavaScript and is intended to be hosted using GitHub Pages.

No installation or server backend is required.